<title>UK: Czech Export Bank ups five-year bond to $250 mln.</title>
<headline>Czech Export Bank ups five-year bond to $250 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to $250 million from $200 million, lead manager J.P. Morgan Securities said on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CZECH EXPORT BANK</p>
<p> AMT	  $250 MLN  COUPON     7.0	 MATURITY    28.MAY.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.419    PAY DATE    28.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  35 BP     REOFFER    99.419    SPREAD	+50 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	BAA1	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  A	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS US/GB/CZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENG	 HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   GROSS UP</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  0.20	PRAECIPUUM  none</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  CZECH REPUBLIC</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
